#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-autotune.rst:87
#: 6f60405d5a5f4ad197b6f89a9363d836
msgid ""
"The :ref:`AUTOTUNE_GN_MAX<AUTOTUNE_GN_MAX>` parameter specifies the "
"maximum response gain to be used to tune the Rate D, Rate P and Angle P "
"gains.  The response gain is the output of the response divided by the "
"input.  It is recommended that 1.8 to 2.0 be used for pitch and roll axes"
" as these axes are typically more lightly damped.  It is recommended that"
" 1.0 to 1.4 be used for the yaw axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-autotune.rst:91
#: c9e4f4b9be804e19a98b396943bb5922
msgid ":ref:`Minimum Test Frequency<AUTOTUNE_FRQ_MIN>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-autotune.rst:93
#: 3b6016a0682547aea77f6210091ee79b
msgid ""
"The :ref:`AUTOTUNE_FRQ_MIN<AUTOTUNE_FRQ_MIN>` parameter specifies the "
"minimum frequency in radians per second used during the dwell or "
"frequency sweeps.  For frequency sweeps, this will be the starting "
"frequency.  The default value is good for helicopters with rotor "
"diameters less than 1.4 meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-autotune.rst:97
#: 333765155d8c4854879f05b4fa8c8649
msgid ":ref:`Maximum Test Frequency<AUTOTUNE_FRQ_MAX>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-autotune.rst:99
#: 3d81f8c9b1994670be0632f5570e7850
msgid ""
"The :ref:`AUTOTUNE_FRQ_MAX<AUTOTUNE_FRQ_MAX>` parameter specifies the "
"maximum frequency in radians per second used during the dwell or "
"frequency sweeps.  For frequency sweeps, this will be the ending "
"frequency.  The default value is fine for helicopters with rotor "
"diameters greater than 1.2 meters.  Consider raising to 100 radians/sec "
"for helicopters with rotor diameters less then 1.2 meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-autotune.rst:103
#: 4118691e65af41b3b7a3130019b90597
msgid ":ref:`Velocity P Gain<AUTOTUNE_VELXY_P>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-autotune.rst:105
#: 27f0b65473c6426bad80ccd983644100
msgid ""
"The :ref:`AUTOTUNE_VELXY_P<AUTOTUNE_VELXY_P>` parameter specifies P gain "
"for velocity feedback.  This aids the AutoTune in maintaining aircraft "
"position during the frequency sweeps and dwells.  It does not apply to "
"``ATC_RAT_xxx_FF`` tuning.  Keep this at 0.1 unless the aircraft is "
"drifting more than 10 meters during the dwell and frequency sweeps.  It "
"only affects position holding while the aircraft is oscillating during "
"these tests.  If it does drift more than 10 meters during the dwell adn "
"frequency sweep tests then increase this parameter but don't increase "
"much beyond 0.2. In between the oscillations, it may drift if the "
"aircraft wasn't properly trimmed for hover.  This gain will not help with"
" that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-autotune.rst:108
#: ef473b94ae5548ab92335ed3b3322478
msgid ":ref:`Maximum Allowable Angular Acceleration<AUTOTUNE_ACC_MAX>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-autotune.rst:110
#: 728889a563924d828acc5f20d2846cc8
msgid ""
"The :ref:`AUTOTUNE_ACC_MAX<AUTOTUNE_ACC_MAX>` parameter specifies maximum"
" allowable angular acceleration in deg/s/s during autotune maneuvers.  "
"This is only available in version Copter-4.6 and subsequent. This "
"parameter limits the requested acceleration.  This does not guarantee the"
" actual aircraft acceleration will be that which was requested.  It is "
"likely that the response will be less than the requested acceleration.  "
"If the response is too low, the resulting analysis may not be good enough"
" for autotune to work well.  If the actual response is much lower, "
"consider increasing the acceleration parameter so that there is a larger "
"response for analysis.  The rate response can be used to estimate the "
"actual acceleration by multiplying the magnitude in deg/s of the "
"oscillatory response by the frequency in rad/s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-autotune.rst:113
#: 5c93c7c5d0af4ab79004e2bb3fdaa647
msgid ":ref:`Maximum Allowable Angular Rate<AUTOTUNE_RAT_MAX>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-helicopter-autotune.rst:115
#: dbe5ba3194a44cbb86623dfba9fbc978
msgid ""
"The :ref:`AUTOTUNE_RAT_MAX<AUTOTUNE_RAT_MAX>` parameter specifies maximum"
" allowable angular rate in deg/s during autotune maneuvers.  This is only"
" available in version Copter-4.6 and subsequent. This parameter limits "
"the requested rate.  This does not guarantee the actual aircraft rate "
"will be that which was requested.  It is likely that the response will be"
" less than the requested acceleration.  If the response is too low, the "
"resulting analysis may not be good enough for autotune to work well.  If "
"the actual response is much lower, consider increasing the rate parameter"
" so that there is a larger response for analysis.  The actual rate can be"
" evaluated from the RATE log message."
msgstr ""

